# GraalVM native-image reachability metadata for javafmt-cli.
#
# Pre-collected reflection/resource hints land here so native-image does not need
# runtime tracing to discover `com.sun.source.tree` service loaders or related JDK
# internals.
#
# How to (re)generate:
#
#   1. Install a GraalVM 21+ JDK (e.g. `sdk install java 21.0.2-graal`) and ensure it
#      is the active toolchain JDK (or export GRAALVM_HOME/JAVA_HOME).
#   2. From the repo root, capture the agent traces against the fixture corpus:
#
#        gradle :javafmt-cli:tracingAgentCapture -Pagent
#
#   3. Merge the captured config into this directory:
#
#        gradle :javafmt-cli:metadataCopy \
#            --task tracingAgentCapture \
#            --dir javafmt-cli/src/main/resources/META-INF/native-image/io.javafmt/javafmt-cli
#
#   4. Review the diff. The agent over-collects — strip anything that looks like
#      junit/assertj/gradle internals before committing.
#   5. Verify the metadata is sufficient:
#
#        gradle :javafmt-cli:nativeCompile
#
# This .gitkeep exists only so the empty directory is tracked. Delete once
# real *-config.json files land alongside it.
